course: dictionary
lesson: 13100
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The clues in the sentence tell you which meaning is right. «The new light fixture in the kitchen is bright and shiny.» A light fixture is a lamp or light that is fixed to the wall or ceiling and stays there.
explain: «Our next fixture is on Saturday at ten o'clock.» Here a fixture is a sports match planned for a certain day. Clues: the word Saturday and the time tell you it is about a planned event, not a thing in a room.
explain: «Mrs Ali is a fixture at the school gate every morning.» Now fixture means a person who is always there. Swap in always there, and the sentence still makes sense. That is how you know you have the right meaning.
fact: Fixture is a noun, and it has more than one meaning.
fact: A fixture can be something fixed in a building, such as a sink, bath, light or cupboard, that is meant to stay there.
fact: In British, Irish, Australian and New Zealand English, a fixture is a sports match planned for a certain day.
fact: A fixture can also be a person or thing that is always there, like a regular at a place.
fact: Useful phrases: «fixture list», «fixtures and fittings», «a permanent fixture».
exercise: «The new light fixture in the kitchen is bright and shiny.» What is a light fixture? | A lamp that you carry around the house | A sports match on Saturday | A light that is always switched off | *Something fixed in a room that stays there
exercise: «Our next fixture is on Saturday at ten o'clock.» In this sentence, fixture means what? | A ceiling fan that spins | A broken window | *A sports match planned for a certain day
exercise: «Mrs Ali is a fixture at the school gate every morning.» What does fixture mean here? | *A person who is always there | A gate that is locked | A morning sports game
test: «Please check the fixture list to see when we play next.» What does fixture list mean? | A list of lost property | *A list of sports matches planned for the season | A list of things fixed to the walls | A shopping list for the kitchen
test: «The sink, the bath and the cupboards are all fixtures in the flat.» What does fixture mean here? | A person who lives in the flat | *Something fixed in the building that stays there | A sports match planned for the weekend
exam: «The old oak tree has been a fixture in the park for two hundred years.» What does fixture mean here? | A sports match planned for a certain day | A tree that someone has lost | *Something that has always been there | A light fixed to the ceiling
